Did you try giving the whole box to the robot?

Did you train the robot to copy the box with just 1 zero in it?

Did you take out the box with 7 zeros in it?

Did you connect the box with 7 zeros to the one with just 1 zeros?

Did you put back the box with 8 zeros after making it?

Did you copy the 1 and drop it on the 7 to keep track of how many
zeros we have added?

Did you remember to press 'Escape' when you were done training the robot?

Did you give the robot the box after training him?

Did you use Dusty to erase the 7, the 24, and the box containing the zeros?

So what I would do if I could is to give the whole box to the robot. Then
I'd train the robot to copy the box with just 1 zero in it. I'd pick up
the box with 7 zeros and drop it on the edge of the box with 1 zero. I'd
pick up the box that should now have 8 zeros and put it back where the
box with 7 zeros was. Then I'd copy the number 1 and drop it on the 7.
I'd press 'Escape' since that's all the robot needs to do. I'd give the
robot the box. When Dusty appears I'd erase the 7 and the box with
7 zeros. I'd give the box back to the robot and wait for him to finish.


